ry-review.js:47 marks the finding a regression. round-policy.test.js:438-469 reproduces this case and passed in receipt index 0 on 63ed6dc. A further instance of the class, where an intermediate reopening is overwritten, remains and is reported as CR6-1.","id":"claude-code/CR5-1","status":"resolved"},{"evidence":"Receipt index 3 on 63ed6dc ran cli/test/self-validation.test.js and cli/test/review-packet.test.js and passed 17 of 17 tests, matching their 9 + 8 top-level tests. A grep of cli/test for review.execute, boundaryReviews, findingObligations, gate.execute and the changed modules finds 20 test files, all covered by receipts 0-3.","id":"claude-code/EV5-1","status":"resolved"}],"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"reintroduction-origin-lost","classStatement":"A finding's later re-reports and present dispositions share one `reopened` history slot that each new one overwrites, so the review that reintroduced it leaves history and qualification takes the origin from a later round.","criterion":"gate:review","evidence":"execution.js:1037 `if (known) Object.assign(known, { open: true, closure: null, reopened: ref })` and :1046 `finding.reopened = ref` replace the single `reopened` reference on every re-report or present disposition. ref stays the first raise (:1038). History selection for an open finding adds only finding.ref, finding.closures and the one finding.reopened (:1053-1055). latestContext and negativeContext (:1023-1027) keep only the latest report per key, so the round-3 reintroducing report is dropped once round 4 reports. In review-findings.js, the round-2 resolution sets resolved:true and origin:null (:90). The round-4 present disposition then sets origin to the round-4 candidate (:94, `if (row.resolved) Object.assign(row, { origin, resolved: false })`). blocks() uses byCandidate.get(origin)?.has(path) (boundary-review.js:47), which is false when round 4 did not touch the path. Base execution.js:1037 set ref to the re-report, so base kept the round-3 report and its origin. This contradicts PROTOCOL.md:333-334 and :345-347, which say a regression keeps the status of the round that first raised it and a reintroduction keeps being judged from its reintroduction. The CR5-1 fix claim lists 'both reopen branches, open-finding selection, prioritization' as swept sites but leaves the single-slot overwrite. round-policy.test.js:438-469 checks only reintroduction followed by one more round. Suggested fix: keep every reopening since the last closure (for example a `reopenings` list) and select it with the closures.","failureScenario":"Medium finding F on app/x.js is raised in round 1 and resolved by both peers in round 2. The round-3 fix changes app/x.js and reintroduces F, and the reviewer re-reports F (it blocks in round 3). The round-4 fix changes only other files, and the reviewers mark F `present`, so round 4 correctly FAILs because the origin is round 3. The round-5 fix again leaves F, and the reviewer marks it present with the other rows passing. Round-5 history now holds the round-1 raise (ref), the round-2 closures and only the round-4 report (reopened). findingObligations moves the origin to the round-4 candidate, whose changed paths exclude app/x.js. F is demoted and the pair qualifies PASS. The base code kept the round-3 report as ref and FAILed this case.","id":"CR6-1","path":"repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/protocol/current/execution.js","severity":"medium"}],"gate":"review","historyAssessment":null,"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The goal (close #144 with cross-round regression tracking, folding in #134) is implemented: sweep-records.js, the roundSchedule integration in boundary-review.js and the review-findings.js prepass and grouping. Interview D6 and DEC-4 record the #134 fold-in as falling out of the same function. Edits to execution.js (checkClaims call, finding-state and history-selection lines, roundPolicy epoch and revision, packet and reuse fields, instruction text) and boundary-review.js remain small, and local-agent-adapters.js is untouched. The disposition record stays extensible for #148 (sweep-records.js:12-15). Agent decisions D1-D7, S2-S14 and DEC-2 to DEC-5 are reversible and stay within the mandate. S13's 'merge authorized by Trent' is an implementer claim the fixed mandate does not grant ('Do not merge'). It describes merging main into the branch, and the candidate shows no merge of the PR. CR6-1 is a defect to fix, not a mandate violation. The PR text constraints cannot be checked because the PR description is not in the bound evidence.","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"Round 6 (hand-back band) review of the whole feature. Base and target are both b0b5fe1; head is 63ed6dc. Because historyGaps is not empty, this is a fresh full assessment. Both open findings from round 5 are resolved. CR5-1: execution.js:1037 and :1046 now keep a finding's closures when it reopens, and :1054 and :1072 carry them for open findings. The new round-policy test 'a reintroduced boundary finding stays a regression in the round after its reintroduction' passed in receipt index 0 on this head. EV5-1: receipt index 3 ran self-validation.test.js and review-packet.test.js, 17 tests, which equals their 9 + 8 top-level tests. One new blocking medium finding is in the same class as CR5-1 (reintroduction-origin-lost). The fix kept closures, but a finding's re-reports and `present` dispositions still go into one `reopened` slot, which the next one overwrites (execution.js:1037, :1046). Take a finding reintroduced by the round-3 fix and marked present again in round 4. By round 5, history no longer holds the review that reintroduced it, so findingObligations takes its origin from round 4. If round 4 did not change that path, the medium regression is demoted and the pair can report PASS. The base code kept the reintroducing review and FAILed this case. execution.js is on this round's regressionPaths, so the finding blocks. Criteria R1-R7 pass on the code and the receipts. Caveats: hosted CI has not run on this head yet (hostedCi is empty). This round's input claims use the old {findingId, claim} shape, an implementer-run artifact of the installed CLI (S10), so no sweep record exists for CR5-1. The PR description is not in the bound evidence. Round 6 qualification also needs the human round-6 decision."}]}